Mon Nov 28 13:13:00 EDT 1998

This src allows you to configure in support for ADB mice. This also
allows you to emulate three button mice on a one button mouse. This
can be done by adding "adb_buttons=X[,keycode_1, keycode_2] to the
vmlinux server line in /mach_servers/bootstrap.conf such as:
/mach_servers/bootstrap.conf such as:
-k ... /dev/.../vmlinux.globegate \"root=/dev/yourroot adb_buttons=..\"

If X is 1, right control/alt will act as button two or three.
If X is 2, it's right control/alt and a mouse click.  You can also
specify the keycodes of what keys will be used instead.

If this doesn't work, try specifying:
-k ... /dev/.../vmlinux.globegate <your mach root> adb_buttons=...

The mach root for SCSI is sd<scsi id number><partition letter 
(0=a 1=b etc)

Then you can use right control/right option as button 2/3 with gpm.
Note, the \s are important.

- Tom Rini
tmrini@ntplx.net

